      "id": "eyd9ffs",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Physical Location"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Haryana is a landlocked state located in north-western India, bounded by Punjab, Himachal Pradesh, Rajasthan, Uttar Pradesh, and Delhi.",
        "The physical landscape is broadly divided into four physiographic zones: the Shivalik Hills, the Yamuna-Ghaggar Plain, the Semi-desert Sandy Plain, and the Aravalli Outliers.",
        "The Yamuna River serves as the only major perennial river, marking the entire eastern border of Haryana with Uttar Pradesh.",
        "The Western Yamuna Canal, originating from Hathnikund/Tajewala in Yamunanagar, is the major backbone of the state's agricultural irrigation network.",
        "The state experiences a subtropical dry continental climate characterized by scorching summers, hot dry winds ('Loo'), and erratic monsoon rainfall."
      ],
      "id": "lr1alz7"
    },
