    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kjyvcus",
      "content": "Haryana is a landlocked state located in the northern part of India. It is surrounded by Punjab and Himachal Pradesh to the north, Uttarakhand and Uttar Pradesh to the east, Rajasthan to the south and southwest, and Delhi to the east (enclave)."
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Yamuna is the only major perennial river of Haryana, defining its eastern boundary with Uttar Pradesh.",
      "id": "t3dzh2d"
    },
